Z||000000||Predator||01-04-2001||09:08 AM||||Anybody out there know of a good mechanic that can work on a Fiero without freaking out when I mention it has been modified with a Turbo kit. I need one in Georgia. I have had no luck finding one that can work on my car. I need to find out what caused one of my head gaskets to blow, and to have it fixed. Surely there is someone out there who can work on this car. The clowns I took it to earlier this week were morons, and I wish they had told me to start that they didn't want to fool with it, and saved us both a lot of headaches. Now my car is not fixed, I know no more than I did what was wrong with it, and I got to spend yesterday afternoon cleaning antifreeze off of my paint job. Thanks in advance for any suggestions.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com/Fiero4.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||01-04-2001||09:29 AM||||What about "Engineered Performance"?<BR>Travis speaks very highly of them. Supposedly there are several Fieros that they maintain.<BR>I'll ask around here for ya'. You might have to come to Douglasville.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Predator||01-04-2001||09:39 AM||||Thanks, I talked to Trav about them before, and I may end up calling them. The only part that bothered me was that he mentioned that they like working on Honda's and such, and probably will give me a hard time about my Fiero. I don't want someone who doesn't want to work on my car working on it. Those are the ones that do half a## job, and I want it fixed right. I am not saying they are bad, but the comments did make me think twice. I have had to many bad mechanics, and I am going to have to pay way to much money to have this fixed to take a chance on a bad job being done. I haven't been able to get in touch with Trav since last week. He has yet to return my phone calls so I am not really sure about it. At this point if the guy is in the state, and is good I will take it there to get it fixed right. Thanks for checking. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com/Fiero4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||01-04-2001||10:12 AM||||What I seem to remember about "Engineered..." is that one of the guys doesn't much care for Fieros, but that the other (Ed, maybe?) is "Fiero tolerant" if not "Fiero friendly". (Reread some of your olders posts. I don't remember exactly.)<BR>I've seen some of their work on some of the Japanese stuff. Looks nice. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Predator||01-04-2001||10:24 AM||||Thanks, I will recheck them out. They do sound good since they do work on Turbo's so maybe they can figure out what caused the problem. As they say I guess it can't hurt to call  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com/Fiero4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||01-04-2001||11:20 AM||||JUST A NOTE:<P>Here in the city we have lots of "Hot Rod" shops, these guys LOVE CARS!!, LOVE to work on CARS! We have speed shops, engine builders, custom car shops, street rods.<P>Why do we always look for "FIERO" repair shops??? Some of these guys have put 351's<BR>in VW Bug's  (j/k)  But you know what I mean<P>Brizio's Street Rods is a well known custom car builder, mostly Roadsters but they do it all. They have had many cars in the Oakland Roadster shows.<P>Gottelli's Speed Shop, They build racing engines/machine shop and own  NHRA dragsters<P>These guys don't mind working on any car! and have a lot of info on just about anything that has to do with a car.<P>Just wondering why these type places are no talked about????<BR>I get info from these guys all the time and have had some work done by them and bought parts from them.<P>Well just a thought??<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||6
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||01-04-2001||12:09 PM||||A quick story.<BR>I was having some work done on one of my<BR>Camaro's at Taylormade Auto Repair and he had to send it out, to Sanderson Headers! Yes they are in SO. San Francisco just up the street from my house and guess what? one of the guys has a V8 Fiero<P>South San Francisco has tons of auto repair shops. You just need to shop around to find what you want??? ||||reg||14
Z||000007||Predator||01-04-2001||12:13 PM||||I wasn't really trying to single out a Fiero Specialist garage. I have called around in my area at several shops, and as soon as I mention Fiero modified with a Turbo Kit they say we can't help you. I called Engineering Performance and talked to Ed just a bit ago and he said he would ask one of his techs if they had time to work on it. They specialize in modifying Jap cars, but have done Fiero's before for Travis. He was very nice and understanding about the whole thing. I by no means was bashing Hot Rod shops. I love Hot Rods. It's just that I don't know of any Hot Rod shops in my area. All the places around where I live are either Tune up/ oil change or tire places. None of which want to take on a major engine diagnosis and repair like what I need. Thanks for the responce though. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com/Fiero4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||2xsess||01-04-2001||12:14 PM||||I know that Joel aka turbo86SE has a mechanic that works on his turbo car all the time, If memory serves right he's a mobile mechanic.Plus he has a Fiero or two himself. I don't know how far he travels but since he has prior knowledge of turbo Fieros might be worth getting in touch with Joel and checking it out.<P>Not trying to cut out anyone(Engineered Performance)||||reg||1
Z||000009||turbo86se||01-04-2001||03:40 PM||||Good suggestion Jeff. I was going to mention the same. I have no doubt that my mechanic, Mike, can fix your engine. I've seen him revive countless Fieros. When I first told him of my turbo-charged 86SE that was dead (cracked manifolds), he couldn't wait to work on it. Though he's not the fastest, he seriously knows his stuff. He's put two 3.8's in Fieros two years ago, and they're running real strong to this day. He is mobile and can pick your car up, I know he's going to NC soon to pick up an '84 coupe to rebuild the engine. If you want to talk to him, let me know and I'll email you my number, I'll be with him all morning tomorrow, we're putting the V6 in my '88 coupe. I can't wait!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||01-05-2001||12:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by turbo86se:<BR><B>...we're putting the V6 in my '88 coupe. I can't wait!!! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Way to go! I know you've been working on that one for a while. <BR>Kinda near and dear to my heart, as I hope to tackle the same project, soon. All I need is time. And a way to reinforce my floor joists so I can hoist the car off the cradle.<P>Predator, Good luck, man.<P>||||reg||1
